                <pb facs="0645" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.73/28: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Philip</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-11T03:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                                1922—3 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 12—5:40
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>15. Department’s 7, of February 6, 5 p.m.<anchor n="45" xml:id="d265-f1"/> Note
                    dated 9th instant from Minister of the Interior embodies following acceptance of
                    proposal based on All America Cables, Incorporated: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Ministry of Government, section two of National Telegraphs and
                            Telephones, Bogotá, March 3, 1922. Be it resolved: The Government of
                            Colombia finds no legal impediment to the renunciation by the All
                            America Cables, Incorporated, which is the subject of the resolution of
                            the 30th of last January, of the company mentioned, and consequently the
                            latter may make the renunciation referred to in the petition, in favor
                            of American and British cable companies; it being <pb facs="0646"
                                n="526" xml:id="pg526"/> thoroughly understood that, according to
                            the contract in force, article 1 of which is copied above, the last
                            [contract?] terminates the 25th day of August, 1924. It is hereby
                            ordered that the above be communicated to the interested party, and that
                            notice thereof be given to His Excellency the Minister of the United
                            States of America as is requested. The Minister, V. M. Salazar.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
